1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,204
Marrek Warehouse: a state-of-the-art locking system, and someone has locked you in.

2
00:00:04,424 --> 00:00:06,173
Here's how the location plays.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,947
Put the Forklift token in The Pit. It's only used if you find the Forklift Keys.

4
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:13,257
Put a Locked token on each exit space.

5
00:00:13,477 --> 00:00:17,254
Set the three Click! Terror cards aside and build the Terror deck as normal.

6
00:00:17,254 --> 00:00:21,429
Then take off the top two cards, shuffle the Click! cards into the rest, and put the

7
00:00:21,429 --> 00:00:22,224
two back on top.

8
00:00:22,444 --> 00:00:24,833
Put the Climb and Leap Action cards in the Tableau.

9
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:29,447
While an exit is Locked, no Victims can be saved there, though you can still move

10
00:00:29,447 --> 00:00:30,147
into the space.

11
00:00:30,367 --> 00:00:34,546
To save Victims you'll need to find ways to unlock exits, such as Bolt Cutters or

12
00:00:34,546 --> 00:00:37,899
the Power Drill, or wait for the timers: the Click! Terror cards.

13
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:40,479
When an exit is unlocked, remove its Locked token.

14
00:00:40,699 --> 00:00:44,602
Each Click! card unlocks its named exit, then you draw the next Terror card.

15
00:00:44,602 --> 00:00:48,812
If a Click! card is discarded by another effect, still unlock the exit, but ignore

16
00:00:48,812 --> 00:00:49,275
the rest.

17
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:53,460
Rack spaces, with this icon, are the tops of the storage racks.

18
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:57,780
Enemies and Victims move to and from them normally, unless a card says otherwise.

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,850
But you have to use the Climb card to get up onto one.

20
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:05,019
You can't use Climb to come down: just use normal movement like Walk or Sprint.

21
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:08,265
Climb and Leap aren't bought like other Action cards.

22
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:12,798
At any time in your Action phase, discard a Walk card to take Climb or Leap into

23
00:01:12,798 --> 00:01:15,440
your hand, or discard a Sprint card to take both.

24
00:01:16,267 --> 00:01:18,784
Climb can only be played when you're next to a Rack space.

25
00:01:19,004 --> 00:01:22,509
Two successes: move up onto the adjacent Rack, losing one Time.

26
00:01:22,509 --> 00:01:25,402
One success: move up, losing two Time. No successes:

27
00:01:25,402 --> 00:01:29,073
lose one health, and the card goes back to your hand to try again.

28
00:01:29,293 --> 00:01:31,213
Victims may follow you when you climb.

29
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:36,172
Leap jumps you directly from one Rack space to another, and Victims may follow.

30
00:01:36,392 --> 00:01:39,379
Two successes costs one Time, one success two Time.

31
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:43,742
With no successes you fall: you must move one space, down to the ground, and lose

32
00:01:43,742 --> 00:01:46,504
two health. Victims who were following don't get hurt;

33
00:01:46,504 --> 00:01:49,113
they just climb down after you to see if you're OK.

34
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:54,255
The middle of the warehouse is The Pit. When someone panics out of it, roll two dice

35
00:01:54,255 --> 00:01:58,061
instead of one to decide where they go, using the Panic numbers around it.

36
00:01:58,867 --> 00:02:03,159
With the Forklift Keys, the Forklift moves with you, though not into Search or Rack

37
00:02:03,159 --> 00:02:07,400
spaces, and for one Time you can safely bring a Victim down from an adjacent Rack.

38
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:12,023
The Supervisor event: when Victims in his space panic, roll one die and move them

39
00:02:12,023 --> 00:02:13,871
all together, Supervisor included.

40
00:02:14,091 --> 00:02:18,357
You Aren't Going Anywhere locks every exit again and shuffles the Click! cards back

41
00:02:18,357 --> 00:02:22,469
in. Smarter Than They Look lets Victims on an exit save themselves the moment it

42
00:02:22,469 --> 00:02:22,880
unlocks.

43
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:28,288
A few tips. Get Victims to an exit before it unlocks, ready to save the moment it

44
00:02:28,288 --> 00:02:28,628
opens.

45
00:02:28,848 --> 00:02:33,033
Use the racks to move around, and keep a spare Walk or Sprint to trade for Climb or

46
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:33,285
Leap.

47
00:02:33,505 --> 00:02:36,197
A Bowling Ball dropped from a rack does three damage.

48
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:36,705
Good luck.

